From 5b31e13d1023a64bf4f8613352e738757b5f56ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:02:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: test the Borg's own grid for stairs in munchkin mode

The adjacent-monster scan in borg_think_dungeon_munchkin() reuses ag,
the pointer to the Borg's own grid, for each neighbour, so after the
scan it points at the last in-bounds neighbour.  The stair tests that
follow read that neighbour's feature: the Borg could press < or > while
not standing on a staircase.  Re-acquire the Borg's own grid before the
tests.

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon.c b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon.c
index 243bb0fd0..4efebabb4 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon.c
@@ -901,6 +901,11 @@ static bool borg_think_dungeon_munchkin(void)
         /* Try to find some stairs */
         if (borg_flow_stair_both(GOAL_FLEE, false))
             return true;
+
+        /* Re-acquire the Borg's own grid: the adjacent-monster scan above
+         * leaves ag pointing at the last neighbour it examined. */
+        ag = &borg_grids[borg.c.y][borg.c.x];
+
         if (ag->feat == FEAT_LESS && !OPT(player, birth_force_descend)) {
             /* Take the Up Stair */
             borg_keypress('<');
